{"type": "message", "id": "fcec1caa", "parentId": "03213934", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T11:02:08.996Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_qefzXcYfd3pnfIm44F73DYRN", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"site:ala.org \\\"Top 10 Most Challenged Books\\\" 2015\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 885,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b0b7f6347d486a6b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2015 Top Ten Most Challenged Books - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b0b7f6347d486a6b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/2015-top-ten-challenged-books/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"01bed21ba272be58\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDuring National Library Week, the Office for Intellectual Freedom publishes the list of Top Ten Most Challenged Books. We collect information from two sources: newspapers and reports submitted by individuals. All challenges are compiled into a database. Reports of challenges culled from newspapers across the country are compiled in the bimonthly Newsletter on Intellectual Freedom and compiled in the Banned Books Week Resource Guide.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"01bed21ba272be58\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 11, 2016\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d311a2d5ffdf1291\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop 10 Most Challenged Books of 2024 | Banned Books\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d311a2d5ffdf1291\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ala.org/bbooks/frequentlychallengedbooks/top10\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0943ef0ae0926822\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEvery year, the American Library Association compiles a list of the Top 10 Most Frequently Challenged Books based on reports from the field and media coverage.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0943ef0ae0926822\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6c7c8c9c93a238b5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop 10 Most Challenged Books Lists\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6c7c8c9c93a238b5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ala.org/advocacy/bbooks/frequentlychallengedbooks/top10/archive\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"38e66284e57bc7d2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe American Library Association condemns censorship and works to ensure free access to information. Every year, the Office for Intellectual Freedom (OIF) compiles a list of the Top 10 Most Challenged Books in order to inform the public about censorship in libraries and schools.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"38e66284e57bc7d2\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c54cef518ff6004e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALSC releases 2015 Summer Reading list | ALA\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c54cef518ff6004e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ala.org/news/2015/04/alsc-releases-2015-summer-reading-list\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"907445fddec2b08e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe American Library Association (ALA) today released the highly anticipated Top 10 Most Challenged Books List.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"907445fddec2b08e\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 16, 2015\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8186a8d1d2c68747\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nA Day in the Li