{"type": "message", "id": "807b2695", "parentId": "251065d5", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T11:02:27.428Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_80KdxrwaEaDEa2NE3uGJGGxZ", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2018 site:oif.ala.org\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 807,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"81895aad2eaf5413\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhy are there 11 most challenged books this year? - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"81895aad2eaf5413\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/oif/?p=17481\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"68a6ced3681d90f8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe ALA Office for Intellectual Freedom tracked 347 challenges to library, school and university materials and services in 2018. View the full list of reasons at ala.org/bbooks/top. Of the 483 books challenged or banned in 2018, below are the Top 11 Most Challenged Books:\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"68a6ced3681d90f8\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 11, 2019\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7716eaa7b9b5469a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nResponses from Authors of the Top 11 Most Challenged Books - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7716eaa7b9b5469a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/oif/?p=17501\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d17dbe0dc5f00b1e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nApril 10, 2019 Ellie Diaz ALA Top Ten Most Frequently Challenged Books, Authors, Banned and Challenged Books · By: Ellie Diaz, Office for Intellectual Freedom Program Officer · On Monday, the American Library Association released the Top 11 Most Challenged Books of 2018 in the State of America’s Libraries Report.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d17dbe0dc5f00b1e\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 10, 2019\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0385a3b892127838\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nField Report 2018 - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0385a3b892127838\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/ALAOIF_FieldReport_2018.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b77cab7cbfe4e1fc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\neveryone, it tends to target · youth; the Top 11 Most · Challenged Books of 2018 are · all intended for an audience · of children or young adults. But there are places where · the light of learning cannot · be extinguished. Libraries, schools, and bookstores keep ·\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b77cab7cbfe4e1fc\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ccd4ce7111050538\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA's Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2020 - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ccd4ce7111050538\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/alas-top-ten-most-challenged-books-of-2020/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"57e1042f6d5c5012\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn 2020, more than 273 books were challenged or banned. Demands to remove books addressing racism and racial justice or those that shared the stories of Black, Indigenous, or people of color grew in number. At the same time, books addressing themes and issues of concern for LGBTQIA+ people continued to dominate the list. Below are the top 10 most challenged books of 2020, and a description of challenges that were reported in the news in 2020, available in the compiled booklet Field Report 2020: Banned &amp; Challenged Books on the ALA Store:\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"57e1042f6d5c5012\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 5, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ee6cfb0c80e71085\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nField Report 2018: Banned and Challenged Books - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ee6cfb0c80e71085\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/field-report-2018/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1ca7b1e5f3ab803d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis annual bibliography includes information on books and resources that are challenged, restricted, removed, or banned. ALA’s Office for Intellectual Freedom compiled sixteen pages filled with descriptions of public challenges and ways to defend the freedom to read.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1ca7b1e5f3ab803d\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 21, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2018 site:oif.ala.org", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 807, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"81895aad2eaf5413\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWhy are there 11 most challenged books this year? - Intellectual Freedom Blog\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"81895aad2eaf5413\">>>", "url": "https://www.oif.ala.org/oif/?p=17481", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"68a6ced3681d90f8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe ALA Office for Intellectual Freedom tracked 347 challenges to library, school and university materials and services in 2018. View the full list of reasons at ala.org/bbooks/top. Of the 483 books challenged or banned in 2018, below are the Top 11 Most Challenged Books:\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"68a6ced3681d90f8\">>>", "published": "April 11, 2019", "siteName": "www.oif.ala.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7716eaa7b9b5469a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nResponses from Authors of the Top 11 Most Challenged Books - Intellectual Freedom Blog\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7716eaa7b9b5469a\">>>", "url": "https://www.oif.ala.org/oif/?p=17501", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d17dbe0dc5f00b1e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nApril 10, 2019 Ellie Diaz ALA Top Ten Most Frequently Challenged Books, Authors, Banned and Challenged Books · By: Ellie Diaz, Office for Intellectual Freedom Program Officer · On Monday, the American Library Association released the Top 11 Most Challenged Books of 2018 in the State of America’s Libraries Report.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d17dbe0dc5f00b1e\">>>", "published": "April 10, 2019", "siteName": "www.oif.ala.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0385a3b892127838\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nField Report 2018 - Intellectual Freedom Blog\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0385a3b892127838\">>>", "url": "https://www.oif.ala.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/ALAOIF_FieldReport_2018.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b77cab7cbfe4e1fc\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\neveryone, it tends to target · youth; the Top 11 Most · Challenged Books of 2018 are · all intended for an audience · of children or young adults. But there are places where · the light of learning cannot · be extinguished. Libraries, schools, and bookstores keep ·\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b77cab7cbfe4e1fc\">>>", "siteName": "www.oif.ala.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ccd4ce7111050538\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nALA's Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2020 - Intellectual Freedom Blog\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ccd4ce7111050538\">>>", "url": "https://www.oif.ala.org/alas-top-ten-most-challenged-books-of-2020/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"57e1042f6d5c5012\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn 2020, more than 273 books were challenged or banned. Demands to remove books addressing racism and racial justice or those that shared the stories of Black, Indigenous, or people of color grew in number. At the same time, books addressing themes and issues of concern for LGBTQIA+ people continued to dominate the list. Below are the top 10 most challenged books of 2020, and a description of challenges that were reported in the news in 2020, available in the compiled booklet Field Report 2020: Banned &amp; Challenged Books on the ALA Store:\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"57e1042f6d5c5012\">>>", "published": "April 5, 2021", "siteName": "www.oif.ala.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ee6cfb0c80e71085\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nField Report 2018: Banned and Challenged Books - Intellectual Freedom Blog\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ee6cfb0c80e71085\">>>", "url": "https://www.oif.ala.org/field-report-2018/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1ca7b1e5f3ab803d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThis annual bibliography includes information on books and resources that are challenged, restricted, removed, or banned. ALA’s Office for Intellectual Freedom compiled sixteen pages filled with descriptions of public challenges and ways to defend the freedom to read.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1ca7b1e5f3ab803d\">>>", "published": "April 21, 2023", "siteName": "www.oif.ala.org"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775300547426}}
{"type": "message", "id": "bf0f8300", "parentId": "807b2695", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T11:02:27.430Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_Kl064odvYam7ltWxtkvHvBaH", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2019 site:oif.ala.org\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 848,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b3f01bafaed6e299\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nA Day in the Life of... ALA's Top 10 Most Challenged Books - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b3f01bafaed6e299\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/a-day-in-the-life-of-alas-top-10-most-challenged-books/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ec518b58ad60c9ab\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDuring National Library Week, the Office for Intellectual Freedom discusses the past year&#x27;s trends. Of the 566 books that were targeted in 2019, here are the most challenged, along with the reasons cited for censoring the books.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ec518b58ad60c9ab\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 30, 2020\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6746560ecdcafe6f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop 10 Challenged Books of 2019 Archives\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6746560ecdcafe6f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/tag/top-10-challenged-books-of-2019/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a61002b98dc26b5d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe Office for Intellectual Freedom of the American Library Association\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a61002b98dc26b5d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a9cde4f0488490b7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTwelve Terrific Challenged LGBTQIAP+ Titles for Kids and Teens - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a9cde4f0488490b7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/twelve-terrific-challenged-lgbtqiap-titles-for-kids-and-teens/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"57b10b50332fd397\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBooks starring a transgender girl (George), a girl crushed out on a boy who likes another boy (Drama), two heroes falling in love after experiencing a fantastical adventure (Prince &amp; Knight), and a male penguin couple who become dads (And Tango Makes Three) also appear. On the 2019 Top Ten list, a record-breaking 8 of the 10 titles were being challenged for this reason. While looking at the decade’s Top Ten Most Challenged Books and more expansive Frequently Challenged Books lists, the idea of creating a new list came to mind.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"57b10b50332fd397\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"June 29, 2020\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"73e0d31f743f6f36\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA Top Ten Most Frequently Challenged Books Archives - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"73e0d31f743f6f36\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/category/ala-top-ten-most-frequently-challenged-books/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"877cd39f07c95263\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nApril 5, 2021April 5, 2021 Jacqui Higgins-Dailey ALA Top Ten Most Frequently Challenged Books, Banned and Challenged Books, Office for Intellectual Freedom · During National Library Week, the Office for Intellectual Freedom discusses the past year’s trends. Of the 566 books that were targeted in 2019, here are the most challenged, along with the reasons cited for censoring the books.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"877cd39f07c95263\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3e690dca47fe0b8f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop Ten Banned Book: Absolutely True Diary of a Part Time Indian - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3e690dca47fe0b8f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/top-ten-banned-book-absolutely-true-diary-of-a-part-time-indian/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2689f1a7dc5bd258\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>The Absolutely True Diary of a Part-Time Indian</strong> was the most-challenged book in the United States from 2010 to 2019 and was named one of the top ten most challenged books in 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013, 2014, 2017, 2018, and 2020.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2689f1a7dc5bd258\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 29, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2019 site:oif.ala.org", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 848, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b3f01bafaed6e299\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nA Day in the Life of... ALA's Top 10 Most Challenged Books - Intellectual Freedom Blog\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b3f01bafaed6e299\">>>", "url": "https://www.oif.ala.org/a-day-in-the-life-of-alas-top-10-most-challenged-books/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ec518b58ad60c9ab\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nDuring National Library Week, the Office for Intellectual Freedom discusses the past year&#x27;s trends. Of the 566 books th