{"type": "message", "id": "7cbf0fd7", "parentId": "57c92ac6", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T11:02:41.852Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_WAUKX6dr1nUP2h4xTn8qtz4W", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"2017 Top Ten Most Challenged Books site:oif.ala.org 2017 top ten most challenged books\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 781,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"77fc033c1528e621\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA Top Ten Most Frequently Challenged Books Archives - Page 3 of 6 - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"77fc033c1528e621\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/category/ala-top-ten-most-frequently-challenged-books/page/3/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2b60bb130a864cb8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA’s Office for Intellectual Freedom released its list of the Top 10 Most Challenged Books of 2016, and as usual, the majority of books are for children and teens. April 26, 2017April 24, 2017 Patricia Peters ALA Top Ten Most Frequently Challenged Books, Banned and Challenged Books, Censorship, Library Bill of Rights, Minors\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2b60bb130a864cb8\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aeb06ad222077fe0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSpotlight on Censorship: 'George' - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aeb06ad222077fe0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/spotlight-censorship-george/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"93395768ecfd742b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGeorge is just one of the five books on the ALA Top Ten list that was challenged because of LGBT content: <strong>Two Boys Kissing (written by David Levithan, who edited George), This One Summer, Drama and I Am Jazz</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"93395768ecfd742b\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 14, 2017\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1c2d79338dda31f9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop Ten Banned Book: Absolutely True Diary of a Part Time Indian - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1c2d79338dda31f9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/top-ten-banned-book-absolutely-true-diary-of-a-part-time-indian/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5662b6397ff000ad\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>The Absolutely True Diary of a Part-Time Indian</strong> was the most-challenged book in the United States from 2010 to 2019 and was named one of the top ten most challenged books in 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013, 2014, 2017, 2018, and 2020.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5662b6397ff000ad\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 29, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c38661391b5be881\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBanned Books Reading Challenge 2017 - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c38661391b5be881\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/oif/?p=8219\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4e6c7371766f0983\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nContributors from the 2017 IF Blog Team: Mack Freeman, April Dawkins and myself… Cathy Collins · (Oscar Wilde, author of the much censored and maligned The Picture of Dorian Gray) ... A children’s book (not picture book) that has been on the top 10 challenges list in the last five years · A young adult novel that has been on the top 10 challenges in the last five years · A children’s book from the most frequently challenged children’s book list\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4e6c7371766f0983\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 6, 2017\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"73d96fef94bd0c6d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSpotlight on Censorship: 'Little Bill' series - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"73d96fef94bd0c6d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/spotlight-censorship-little-bill-series/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b4c48293c318fc5d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFor the first time, one of the Top Ten Challenged Books titles was challenged solely because of the author. At the end of 2015, Bill Cosby was charged with drugging and sexually assaulting a woman at his home in 2004 — the first criminal charges brought against the comedian and author. In response, the Little Bill series was threatened with removal from communal shelves and reading prizes, making it No. 9 on the Top Ten Challenged Books of 2016.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b4c48293c318fc5d\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 11, 2017\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "2017 Top Ten Most Challenged Books site:oif.ala.org 2017 top ten most challenged books", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 781, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"77fc033c1528e621\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nALA Top Ten Most Frequently Challenged Books Archives - Page 3 of 6 - Intellectual Freedom Blog\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"77fc033c1528e621\">>>", "url": "https://www.oif.ala.org/category/ala-top-