 Celebrating National Library Week 2021 · Monday, April 5: State of America’s Libraries Report released, including Top Ten Frequently Challenged Books of 2020.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3fedf49a4cccfe30\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 5, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6e89725abe52d236\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDefending Books in a Middle School: an Interview with Librarian Gina Schaarschmidt - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6e89725abe52d236\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/q-facing-middle-school-book-challenge/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"91a2b18c2cfdee43\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn celebration of National Library Week and its theme “Libraries Lead,” the Intellectual Freedom Blog is highlighting the voices and experiences of fierce librarians who have defended the right to read in the past year. Learn more about the Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2017 and this year’s Banned Books Week theme “Banning Books Silences Stories; Speak Out!” at ala.org/bbooks/NLW-Top10.)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"91a2b18c2cfdee43\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 8, 2018\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"800a64f8126c882b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop Ten Banned Book: Absolutely True Diary of a Part Time Indian - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"800a64f8126c882b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/top-ten-banned-book-absolutely-true-diary-of-a-part-time-indian/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cfdeb907958a17c5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>The Absolutely True Diary of a Part-Time Indian</strong> was the most-challenged book in the United States from 2010 to 2019 and was named one of the top ten most challenged books in 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013, 2014, 2017, 2018, and 2020.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cfdeb907958a17c5\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 29, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"598ea38e9805d2f7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA Top Ten Most Frequently Challenged Books Archives - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"598ea38e9805d2f7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.oif.ala.org/category/ala-top-ten-most-frequently-challenged-books/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5db9fdca6cce664d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIf number of challenges are a marker of the serious themes of a book, Sherman Alexie’s The Absolutely True Diary of a Part-Time Indian is worthy of close attention as one of the top ten most challenged books of all time. The novel features a teenager born with disabilities including encephalitis, who has grown up on a reservation in Spokane, Washington.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5db9fdca6cce664d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.oif.ala.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "site:oif.ala.org \"Top Ten Most Challenged Books\" 2017 #1", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 816, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"deee2c31f7d57227\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2017\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"deee2c31f7d57227\">>>", "url": "https://www.oif.ala.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/ALAOIF_Field-Report-2017.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"adb0d0f1d7c5adcc\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTOP TEN · CHALLENGED BOOKS · OF 2017 · #1 <strong>THIRTEEN REASONS WHY</strong> · by Jay Asher · REASON: suicide · #2 THE ABSOLU