{"type": "message", "id": "8a06da4a", "parentId": "0d8e33c8", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T11:05:02.923Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_OnOslx4JOXqXw27S9OzY8QjH", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"site:ala.org/bbooks \\\"Censorship by the Numbers\\\" 2017 top ten most challenged\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 4,\n  \"tookMs\": 745,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fcb2f46078f862d1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop 10 and Frequently Challenged Books Archive | Banned Books\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fcb2f46078f862d1\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ala.org/bbooks/frequentlychallengedbooks/top10/archive\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6e7b17f6d09db94d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAnd Tango Makes Three written by Peter Parnell and Justin Richardson and illustrated by Henry Cole Returning after a brief hiatus from the Top Ten Most Challenged list, this ALA Notable Children’s Book, published in 2005, was challenged and labeled because it features a same-sex relationship. I Am Jazz written by Jessica Herthel and Jazz Jennings and illustrated by Shelagh McNicholas This autobiographical picture book co-written by the 13-year-old protagonist was challenged because it addresses gender identity. Download the Censorship by the Numbers 2017 infographic.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6e7b17f6d09db94d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dd3c762532f921cf\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCensorship by the Numbers | Banned Books\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dd3c762532f921cf\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ala.org/bbooks/censorship-numbers\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9b43e42a57828a79\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLast year, <strong>2,452 unique titles</strong> were challenged, the third highest number ever documented by ALA and significantly exceeding the annual average of 273 unique titles over the period from 2001–2020. Scroll to the bottom of this page for a PDF version of Censorship by the Numbers.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9b43e42a57828a79\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f231b4e0f0bf6d0d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop 10 Most Challenged Books of 2024 | Banned Books\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f231b4e0f0bf6d0d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ala.org/bbooks/frequentlychallengedbooks/top10\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"50ea368a85a102ca\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEvery year, the American Library Association compiles a list of the Top 10 Most Frequently Challenged Books based on reports from the field and media coverage. ... The American Library Association condemns censorship and works to defend each person&#x27;s right to read under the First Amendment and to ensure free access to information.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"50ea368a85a102ca\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0d8153a0f815cb32\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFree Downloads | Banned Books\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0d8153a0f815cb32\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ala.org/bbooks/bannedbooksweek/ideasandresources/freedownloads\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8793fced6dc2767c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDownload social media assets for the Top 10 Most Challenged Books from the galleries below by clicking on the icon in